<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">6 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 6 February, from 1481 to 1952.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-inquisition" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spanish-inquisition.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1481">1481 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">545 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Spanish Inquisition holds its first auto-da-fé in Seville</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Six people convicted of secretly practising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaism">Judaism</a> were burned at the stake after a public ceremony in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a>. Autos-da-fé became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-inquisition">Inquisition</a>'s most notorious public ritual.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1579">1579 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">447 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Domingo de Salazar becomes the first bishop of Manila</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-order">Dominican friar</a> Domingo de Salazar was appointed the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a>, then newly annexed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>; he served until 1594.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-order">Dominican Order</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1685">1685 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">341 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James II becomes king on the death of Charles II</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Charles II died at Whitehall and his Catholic brother succeeded as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-england">James II of England</a> and VII of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>. Fears of a Catholic dynasty led to his overthrow in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution">Glorious Revolution</a> of 1688.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1778">1778 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">248 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">France signs an alliance with the United States</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benjamin-franklin">Benjamin Franklin</a> and his fellow commissioners signed treaties of alliance and commerce with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. French troops, money and naval power proved decisive in the war for independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1820">1820 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">206 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First American Colonization Society settlers sail for Africa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The ship Elizabeth left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> carrying 86 free Black Americans bound for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>. Their settlement efforts led to the founding of Liberia.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1840">1840 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">186 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Waitangi signed in New Zealand</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British officials and more than 40 Māori chiefs signed the treaty at Waitangi. Differences between its English and Māori texts over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> remain central to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> law and politics.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British women over thirty win the vote</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Representation of the People Act gave the vote to women over 30 who met property qualifications, about 8.4 million women. Equal voting rights with men followed in 1928.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1952">1952 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">74 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Elizabeth II becomes Queen on the death of George VI</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The 25-year-old princess learned of her father's death while in Kenya. She reigned for 70 years, the longest of any British monarch, until her death in 2022.</p></div></li></ol>
